# Base-neutral names for the dependencies the srcpkgs/*/template files declare (depends, makedepends,
# hostmakedepends). One line per name a template uses:
#   VOID-NAME | NEUTRAL NAME | WHAT IT IS NEEDED FOR
# build/install/deps.sh joins each template's lists with this table into the dependencies report; a name a
# template declares that is not here stops the report (so a dependency added to a template later is described).
# A neutral name of "-" marks a Void-only package that has no counterpart on another base.
#
# ---- runtime: the base system
base-files | base filesystem layout | /etc and /usr skeleton, os-release
ncurses | ncurses | terminal handling for the console tools
coreutils | GNU coreutils | every shell script
findutils | GNU findutils | the tools' and installer's scripts
diffutils | GNU diffutils | config merges in ribbon-update
libgcc | libgcc (GCC runtime) | C/C++ binaries
dash | dash | /bin/sh
bash | bash | ribbon-theme, ribbon-tools scripts
grep | GNU grep | every shell script
gzip | gzip | compressed files, initramfs
file | file (libmagic) | file type detection
sed | GNU sed | every shell script
gawk | GNU awk | the dinit layer, ribbon-tools
less | less | pager
util-linux | util-linux | mount, lsblk, findmnt, zramctl, flock
which | which | scripts locating programs
tar | tar | archives, the installer
man-pages | Linux man-pages | manual pages
mdocml | mandoc | man reader
shadow | shadow (useradd, passwd) | accounts, the installer, Settings Users
e2fsprogs | e2fsprogs | ext4 data drives, fsck
btrfs-progs | btrfs-progs | the btrfs root, snapshots
xfsprogs | xfsprogs | XFS data drives
f2fs-tools | f2fs-tools | F2FS data drives
dosfstools | dosfstools | the EFI system partition
exfatprogs | exfatprogs | exFAT drives
ntfs-3g | ntfs-3g | NTFS drives, the installer's Windows detection
procps-ng | procps-ng | ps, pkill, sysctl
tzdata | tzdata (IANA time zones) | the clock, Settings Date & Time
pciutils | pciutils | GPU detection (ribbon-gpu, ribbon-hw)
usbutils | usbutils | lsusb in ribbon-doctor
iana-etc | IANA /etc/services and /etc/protocols | networking
kbd | kbd | console keymaps and fonts
iproute2 | iproute2 | ip, the dinit network setup
iputils | iputils | ping
iw | iw | Wi-Fi regulatory and device queries
wpa_supplicant | wpa_supplicant | Wi-Fi for NetworkManager
xbps | - (Void's package manager) | ribbon-update, ribbon-tools' xbps-install wrapper (Void only)
nvi | nvi (vi) | the console editor
sudo | sudo | admin commands, the sudoers drop-ins
wifi-firmware | Wi-Fi firmware | wireless cards
traceroute | traceroute | network diagnosis
ethtool | ethtool | network diagnosis
kmod | kmod | modprobe, modules-load
eudev | udev (eudev or systemd-udev standalone) | device events, udev-trigger
removed-packages | - (Void's removed-packages) | removes obsolete Void packages (Void only)
glibc-locales | glibc locales | LANG=en_US.UTF-8
bash-completion | bash-completion | shell completion
dracut | dracut | the initramfs, ribbon's dracut modules
cryptsetup | cryptsetup | encrypted disks
lvm2 | lvm2 | LVM volumes
limine | Limine boot loader | the default boot loader
efibootmgr | efibootmgr | EFI boot entries
snapper | snapper | btrfs snapshots
NetworkManager | NetworkManager | networking, Settings Network
chrony | chrony | time sync, Settings Date & Time
cronie | cronie | cron jobs
nftables | nftables | the firewall (Ribbon's ruleset, /usr/share/ribbon/nftables.conf)
apparmor | AppArmor userspace | confinement profiles
linux-firmware-amd | linux-firmware (AMD) | AMD GPUs and CPUs
linux-firmware-intel | linux-firmware (Intel) | Intel GPUs and CPUs
linux-firmware-network | linux-firmware (network) | network cards
linux-firmware-broadcom | linux-firmware (Broadcom) | Broadcom Wi-Fi
